Add a cargo-fuzz target `ndjson` (upstream has none)

A lean4export NDJSON stream, checked as `con-ron FILE.ndjson` does in check_main
(con_ron_core::driver::check_main since upstream moved the driver into the core):
reserved pins, built-in prelude, streaming parse (parse_source over the input in
CHUNK_SIZE chunks, as FileChunks reads the file), prepare_d, the embedded Nat-op
pins and check_phase in the default --verified mode on one worker (build_index,
the frozen tier, every record's run_job in order from one worker_state until the
first failure, as the pool does with one worker). The pins and the prelude state
are built once from a static constructor; each input takes the state wasmfuzz's
snapshot restores, other runners rebuild it after the first input.
Upstream: none (no fuzz targets upstream, checked 2026-11-24).

